---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;

const title =
  "TACET — cost-amortised reasoning via self-distilling neuro-symbolic cascades";
const description =
  "A three-tier cascade that migrates a streamed workload off the LLM and onto checkable tiers, with replayable Datalog proof trees. Measured cost amortisation, and the boundaries where it stops working.";
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <h1>Cost-amortised reasoning via self-distilling neuro-symbolic cascades</h1>

  <p class="lede">
    From knowledge-graph QA to regulatory-compliance checking. A sound Datalog tier, a
    calibrated link predictor, and an LLM teacher — with an online distillation loop that
    moves the teacher's answers down into the cheap tiers as the workload streams.
  </p>

  <div class="actions">
    <a class="btn" href={`${base}paper/`}>Read the paper</a>
    <a class="btn secondary" href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20621240">Zenodo (DOI)</a>
    <a class="btn secondary" href="https://github.com/n24q02m/tacet">Source code</a>
  </div>

  <h2>What is measured</h2>

  <div class="scroller">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Setting</th><th>Result</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>MetaQA, real Grok 4.3 teacher, matched accuracy</td>
          <td class="num">2.8x / 5.1x</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>GDPR compliance (PrivaCI), three frontier teachers</td>
          <td class="num">1.5-2.1x</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Oracle teacher, unseen heads</td>
          <td class="num">87% fewer calls</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p>
    The saving under a real teacher comes from answer reuse. The distinctive claim — that a
    synthesised rule generalises past a cache — is teacher-quality-gated, and the paper says
    where it does not hold.
  </p>

  <h2>What did not work</h2>

  <p>
    Roughly half the paper is negative results, reported because they bound the method rather
    than decorate it:
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li>
      A graph forward-dynamics forecaster, kept as a documented negative rather than dropped.
    </li>
    <li>
      Label-free promotion of mined rules: neither agreement with the teacher nor multi-sample
      self-consistency works, because the teacher's error on these workloads is systematic, and
      a majority vote cancels random noise rather than systematic error.
    </li>
    <li>
      Cross-teacher "distillability" turns out to be confounded by answer length, so no ranking
      is reported and no benchmark is built on one.
    </li>
    <li>
      An earlier version excluded a third of the grid and blamed teacher verbosity. Both halves
      were wrong; the current version reports the full grid and records the misattribution.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Citing</h2>

  <p>
    The version of record is the Zenodo deposit under concept DOI
    <code>10.5281/zenodo.20621240</code>, which always resolves to the latest version.
    <code>CITATION.cff</code> in the repository is kept in step with it.
  </p>
</Base>
